8. Production considerations
The pattern is useful, but there are a few things to handle in a production application.
Consideration	                            Why it matters
Duplicate payment methods	                 toUnmodifiableMap() throws an exception if two processors return the same key.
Unsupported methods	                          The Factory should return a clear error or use an explicit fallback policy.
Bean initialization	                         The map is built when the Factory is constructed.
Payment gateway failures	                  Processor implementations should handle gateway errors, timeouts, and transaction status carefully.
Payment method validation	                Validate the requested method before attempting processing.
One important distinction: the Factory selects the payment processor; it does not guarantee that the payment is successful.
